From: dtrace.nix maintainers
Subject: bpf: emit program disassembly only from the construction pass

The bounded-memory change adds an analysis pass that constructs and immediately
frees each program before the real construction pass.  Disassembly is an output
side effect, not part of that analysis, so emitting it there duplicates every
program listing.  Keep diagnostics in the real construction/linking pass.

--- a/libdtrace/dt_bpf.c
+++ b/libdtrace/dt_bpf.c
@@ -1283,8 +1283,6 @@
 		dp = dt_construct(dtp, prp, cflags, NULL);
 		if (dp == NULL)
 			return -1;
-
-		DT_DISASM_PROG(dtp, cflags, dp, stderr, NULL, prp->desc);
 
 		dt_difo_free(dtp, dp);
 	}
